     "title": "Animal groups",
     "md": "**Mammals** have hair or fur and feed their babies with **milk** (goat, cow, bat, human). **Birds** have feathers, wings and lay eggs (hen, parrot). **Reptiles** have dry scaly skin and lay eggs (lizard, snake, crocodile). **Amphibians** have moist skin and begin life in water (frog). **Fish** live in water, with gills, fins and scales. **Insects** have **6 legs** and 3 body parts (ant, bee, housefly)."
