     "title": "What animals eat and where they live",
     "md": "**Herbivores** eat plants (goat, cow, elephant). **Carnivores** eat other animals (lion, snake, eagle). **Omnivores** eat both (human, pig, chicken). A **habitat** is the place where an animal lives: forest, river, savanna, house. A spider has 8 legs, so it is **not** an insect."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Calling a bat a bird: it has fur and feeds its young with milk, so it is a **mammal**.\n- Saying that a spider is an insect (6 legs; spiders have 8).\n- Calling a whale or a dolphin a fish: they are mammals.\n- Thinking that all snakes are dangerous: many are harmless, but keep away from all wild snakes."
    },
